{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unreal-empathetic-illadopsis","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Summary\n\n`_decorate_outbound_comment` (`outbound_comments.py`) appends `RECONCILER_MARKER` AFTER the comment body. The outbound comment-limit truncation (`adapters/jira/comment_limits.py`, `_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX = \\\" … [truncated by reconciler]\\\"`) then cuts the composed text at the 32767-char limit, which removes the trailing marker paragraph.\n\n## Impact\n\nA comment whose body exceeds the limit lands in Jira with NO marker. That comment is then:\n- unrecognisable as the reconciler's own echo on the inbound side (the loop-breaker at `inbound_collection_diffs.py` tests for the marker in the body text), and\n- unrecognisable to any tooling that identifies bot-authored comments by the marker.\n\n## Evidence (live)\n\nFound during the duplicate-comment cleanup (`darkish-enormous-raptors` / `76b2-4b5f-5682-45e5`). 836 Jira comments across REB-1567 (418), REB-1931 (278) and REB-2605 (140) are marker-less. Each is authored by the bridge bot accountId `712020:6471376f-4e5e-4ed2-8c05-330827bc387e`, is exactly 32767 rendered chars, ends in `_TRUNCATION_SUFFIX`, and repeats ~139 times identically. They had to be excluded from the marker-based cleanup as non-candidates.\n\n## Expected vs Actual\n\n- Expected: every outbound comment carries the marker regardless of body length.\n- Actual: any comment over the limit loses it.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Outbound truncation reserves room for the marker — truncate the BODY to (limit - len(marker) - len(suffix)) and append the marker after truncating, so the composed text is <= the limit AND ends with the marker.\n- [ ] Unit test: a body longer than the limit produces an outbound payload that is <= the limit and whose rendered text contains RECONCILER_MARKER. RED on current code.\n- [ ] Unit test: the truncation suffix is still present on a truncated body (the existing truncation contract is not broken).","id":"5931-78a3-95d2-44cd","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Outbound comment truncation drops the RECONCILER_MARKER, defeating the loop-breaker for >32767-char comments"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1787267840343662001,"uuid":"a91a79bc-3760-4a1b-8250-8bb8931dd67d"}